body:
The copy error handling silently logs to console without providing user feedback. When clipboard access fails (common in non-HTTPS environments or when permissions are denied), users won't know why the copy didn't work.

Consider adding visual feedback for errors, such as showing a toast notification or changing the icon to an error state temporarily.
```suggestion
      console.error('Failed to copy:', err);
      if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
        window.alert('Failed to copy to clipboard. Please check your browser permissions and try again.');
      }
```
